@Including files
.
=INCLUDING FILES
.
.#INCLUDE "NAME" compiles the file NAME in place of its line. The compiler
.reads NAME, then the lines after the #INCLUDE.
.
:' TOOLS.UXI holds SUB TWICE(N) AS WORD
:#INCLUDE "TOOLS.UXI"
:PRINT TWICE(21)
.
.  - The file is read from the same drive as the source.
.  - An included file cannot include another file.
.  - An error in an included file reports the line of the #INCLUDE, with the
.    file name and its own line: SYNTAX ERROR (LIB.UXI 2).
.
.See Strings, Subroutines.
.
